We start by initializing an 8x8 checkerboard with alternating black and white squares. Then, we will iterate over all possible squares of sizes 1x1 to 8x8 and count the number of black squares in each square. If the number of black squares is at least 5, we add that square to our list of valid squares. Finally, we'll count the number of such valid squares.

